# Labels for the bundled FBE decrypt binaries in the recovery ramdisk.
#
# The twrp-common init.recovery.qcom_decrypt(.fbe).rc service definitions run
# these under an explicit "seclabel u:r:recovery:s0", so the domain transition
# does not depend on these exec-type labels; they are kept for correctness and
# to match the binaries' final /system/bin location in the recovery ramdisk.
#
# NOTE (first decrypt-iteration item): qseecomd labeling and any AVC denials
# raised while starting the crypto services must be resolved from the on-device
# /tmp/recovery.log of the first one-slot decrypt test. Do not guess additional
# allow rules blind — add them from real denials.

# qseecomd intentionally NOT labeled here: its Qualcomm exec type
# (qseecomd_exec) is not defined in the OrangeFox recovery sepolicy, and
# referencing an undefined type breaks the file_contexts build. It runs under
# the explicit recovery seclabel from the rc; add a label only if a real AVC
# denial on the first on-device decrypt test proves one is needed.
/system/bin/android\.hardware\.keymaster@4\.0-service-qti     u:object_r:hal_keymaster_default_exec:s0
/system/bin/android\.hardware\.gatekeeper@1\.0-service-qti    u:object_r:hal_gatekeeper_default_exec:s0
